          <text id="/data/results_group/res_severe_dehydration:label">
            <value>Severe Dehydration</value>
          </text>
          <text id="/data/results_group/res_severe_dehydration_action:label">
            <value>Place Levine tube, and use siringe to provide ORS through the tube, Then Refer URGENTLY to hospital with mother giving frequent sips of ORS on the way. Advise the mother to continue breastfeeding.</value>
          </text>
          <text id="/data/results_group/res_some_dehydration:label">
            <value>Some Dehydration</value>
          </text>
          <text id="/data/results_group/res_some_dehydration_action:label">
            <value>Give ORS, zinc supplements, and food for some dehydration (Plan B - DOSING). If child also has a severe classification: Refer URGENTLY to hospital with mother giving frequent sips of ORS on the way. Advise the mother to continue breastfeeding. Go to hospital in 5 days if not improving.</value>
          </text>
          <text id="/data/results_group/res_no_dehydration:label">
            <value>No Dehydration</value>
          </text>
          <text id="/data/results_group/res_no_dehydration_action:label">
            <value>Give 4 packets of ORS to go home with as well as zinc supplements, and food to treat diarrhea at home (Plan A - DOSING). Advise mother when to go to hospital immediately.</value>
          </text>
          <text id="/data/results_group/res_persistent_diarrhea:label">
            <value>Persistent Diarrhea</value>
          </text>
          <text id="/data/results_group/res_persistent_diarrhea_action:label">
            <value>ORS Treat dehydration before referral unless the child has another severe classification (DOSING). Refer to hospital.</value>
          </text>
          <text id="/data/results_group/res_dysentery:label">
            <value>Dysentery</value>
          </text>
          <text id="/data/results_group/res_dysentery_action:label">
            <value>Give trimetoprim sulfate (TMS) for 3 days (200/40 mg per 5 ml – 4 a 5 mg per kg per day in two doses) and metronidazole 250mg/5ml suspension – 20 mg par kg par jour en trois doses). Breastfeeding. Treated water.</value>
          </text>
          <text id="/data/results_group/res_gastritis:label">
            <value>Gastritis</value>
          </text>
          <text id="/data/results_group/res_gastritis_action:label">
            <value>Give ORS. Metoclopramide IM – dosing: 0.1 mg par kg max 0.5 mg. Antacid: Litacid Gel. Counseling on good feeding practices: no spicy food, no salty food, no tomato sauce or mayonaise, regular small meals. Soup, vegetables, soup. Recommendation for hygiene: washing hands, no raw food, washing fruit with soap.</value>
          </text>
          <text id="/data/results_group/res_cholera:label">
            <value>Risk of Cholera</value>
          </text>
          <text id="/data/results_group/res_cholera_action:label">
            <value>IV fluid – Ringer/lactate if severely dehydrated. ORS. Refer to cholera treatment center or hospital.</value>
          </text>
          <text id="/data/null_results_group:label">
            <value>No Conditions Met</value>
          </text>
